WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.270
My fangs will tear you apart, Earth Engine!

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.440
What's that?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.900
A planetary sign?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.290
Albion!

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.550
What?

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.600
Albion... What are you doing?!

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.970
Teppei, is that you?

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.700
Albion appeared...

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.030
And it interfered with my descent.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:04.910
What?

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.210
Something bad is about to happen.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.040
We need to look into this.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.770
Having a summer break like this is a pretty nice change of pace.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.900
Hey, Pitz.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.400
Want a watermelon seed?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.280
Hana's got you too worried to eat, huh?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.500
Just like Daichi?

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.790
I definitely am worried about Hana...

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.540
But what about Teppei? Is he going to be okay?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.920
You getting anxious over the situation isn't going to help them.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.340
Fair point.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.270
Belly Button...

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.600
Belly Button Forte!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.280
Well? What do you think?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.780
Wh-What do I think? What are you doing?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:31.250
This is the beautiful, adorable Akari showing you her belly button

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.620
as a magic spell to lift your spirits!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.540
Belly Button Forte!

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.340
See? You feel better now, don't you?

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.880
Yeah... A little, I suppose.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.640
Very well then!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.720
We're going to bust our way in!

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.310
Last night's earthquake was caused by the ship's movement on the sea floor.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.980
We believe she used her own body as an energy relay circuit

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.860
to activate the main systems of the Machine Goodfellow <i>Aramusha</i>.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.320
We know that her body contains an unknown type of cellular organelle

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.370
not regularly found in <i>Homo sapiens</i>.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.460
We've hypothesized that the energy she used

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.090
may be a variant of the Orgone energy stored on the Blume.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:28.800
These are the results of the mental health exam, the forensic psychiatry analysis,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.970
and the thought examination system that we conducted this morning.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.690
He was very cooperative with all the tests.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.610
Good morning, Teppei.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.860
That Machine Goodfellow you used last night

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.450
was covertly removed from Macbeth Enterprises during the Kanda incident.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.660
At the same time as you, in fact...

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.090
We were aware that it was able to recognize you specifically.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.550
That it was designed to be your own personal Neural Maneuver System.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.630
I didn't know.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.890
Yes, that was our intent until yesterday.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.770
Macbeth Enterprises

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.350
ostensibly developed it as a man-machine interface

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:26.610
to be used in the latest mobile weaponry, but early on we realized it had a much greater function...

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:35.200
No, that it had actually been developed for an entirely different purpose.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.330
But we didn't know then what it was for.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.210
Were you controlling that Kill-T-Gang Type-3

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.550
that appeared in the Earth Engine's combat zone?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.760
No, I don't think you were <i>controlling</i> it...

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:59.810
You <i>were</i> that Type-3 that even now continues to drift through Alpha sector.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.270
That's right, isn't it?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.900
Thank you... That's all.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.410
He was the Kill-T-Gang itself?
What do you mean?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.620
Until yesterday,

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:23.750
Teppei had the mental profile of a 17-year-old Japanese teenager.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:28.460
When I looked at him, I never doubted it for a second.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.680
But what about now?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:35.680
I'd be very interested in finding out what he can tell us

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.350
now that he's become a Kill-T-Gang.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.600
Knowledge of this could be very dangerous.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:44.360
It is of grave significance in determining the course of action from here on out.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:46.900
Commander!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:55.120
Until we've learned more, this matter is classified top-secret.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.200
Even where headquarters is involved.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.210
You of course realize that that decision is not within

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.710
your authority to make, don't you?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.460
The way I see it right now,

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:14.470
Teppei's Kill-T-Gang saved the Earth Engine.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.390
You're not headed back to the base?

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.390
We need to eat first, of course.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.560
You just ate that entire watermelon...

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.430
Nope, that didn't count.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.560
How about a crêpe? They're delicious!

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.480
Want one?

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.360
Okay, I'll take a banana crêpe.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.070
I'll have a mango crêpe.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.900
Coming right up.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.660
You're going to squander the magic of your belly button if you're always showing it.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.660
Or maybe you won't?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.540
Here you go.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.830
Thanks!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.090
Want some, Pitz?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.800
Here you go.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.720
Thanks.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:38.970
Hmm?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.310
You shouldn't waste food.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.390
That's right.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.270
You've got a pretty big trailer.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.480
I travel around Japan selling crêpes.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.320
Today's my first time on this island.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.940
The wind feels good here, doesn't it?

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.150
The wind?

00:09:59.110 --> 00:09:59.950
Does it?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.050
Can we head in?

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.880
Oh, hang on just a second...

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.810
All right, you're cleared for entrance.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.440
Those look tasty.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.900
They're fantastic!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.530
Hana's currently undergoing a physical exam at the medical center.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.900
Where's Teppei?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.070
Room 45, block C.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.740
But that's the interrogation room...

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.910
Stop touching things without permission!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.370
Oh, that place...

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.420
It's so depressing in there.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.380
Fine... You can see him.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.230
Aren't you being a bit soft?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:47.100
When I was a kid, I was kind of proud of this.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:52.980
But once I realized how strange being able to make a rainbow appear over my hand was...

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.110
I avoided doing it anymore.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.570
I pretended I couldn't do it.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.610
I dream every night,

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.990
but really it's when I'm awake that I feel like I'm dreaming.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:15.420
Somehow I knew that the real me wasn't the person I am now.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.170
But you're still you, right?

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.880
Thank you. You saved my life.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.350
And you really surprised me this time!

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.370
I heard your crêpes are really good.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:57.130
But you can't enter without clearance... Sorry.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.590
You can't just give us permission yourself?

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.050
Maybe we'll just let ourselves in, then!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.640
I can't do anything about the base's security measures!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.060
I mean, you can't just fool a machine, you know?

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.850
If you go past here, something scary will happen.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.100
Well, I wouldn't want that.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:20.980
What?

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.070
What's going on?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.200
It's easy to fool machines.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:33.500
Too easy.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:35.370
Too easy.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:40.840
My cute little bunny has taken over their defense system.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.520
This is...

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.360
What is this?

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.070
What's going on?!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.950
The base's antipersonnel defenses have been deactivated...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:11.830
What?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.080
Something's happening in C block!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.170
They're here for Teppei?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.750
Rita, Thunder, you're with me!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.220
A direct attack on our base?

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.890
Could it be Salty Dog?
Or maybe the Ark Faction?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.560
No, I haven't told HQ about Teppei yet.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.070
If they're after Teppei, that means...

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.490
I have a very bad feeling about this.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.470
You're Alaya, right?

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.770
No... I don't use that name.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.610
Well, your avatar name doesn't really matter, anyway.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.280
You are Albion, aren't you?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.280
His memories haven't returned?

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.110
That's impossible...

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.870
He abreacted into the Kill-T-Gang.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:33.450
Isn't that right?

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.160
I've been looking for you.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.830
You had me really worried, too.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.790
Why did you interfere yesterday?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.330
Have you gone rogue?

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.040
No way.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:51.220
Teppei!

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.180
Don't move.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.560
Where's Daichi?

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.810
Over there!

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:58.930
Daichi!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.350
Throw down your weapons and surrender!

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.900
You're outnumbered!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.270
I'd rather not waste food.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.110
Yeah...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:12.490
We will be eating them eventually.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.200
They're...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:21.870
Daichi!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.960
Thank goodness, he's alive.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.460
Then, are you two...

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.670
Who are you, anyway?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.970
The crêpe seller, right?

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:39.350
I am the Planetary Gear Amarok.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.560
And I'm the Planetary Gear Malkin.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.730
Do you regard Earth's humans as food?

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.530
Yeah, that's the gist of it.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.240
But that's what the people of this world want, anyway.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.120
I'd rather not waste food,

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.460
but if you want to fight, I won't hold back!

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.460
Logical, logical...

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.720
Be careful. The antipersonnel defenses are coming back online.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:19.100
Logical, logical!
Bye-bye, naughty little rabbit!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.140
Okay!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.150
Hang in there!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.320
My rabbit's been contained?!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.280
This is starting to get exciting...

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.740
Then let's run like rabbits!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.320
Wait!

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:41.450
Stop!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.120
What's that?!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.550
A mobile suit?

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.760
Let's wreak some havoc, <i>Tenrousei!</i>

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.020
That's their weapon?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.410
Stop it!

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.210
Albion...

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.960
Stop doing this!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.720
It's me you want, right?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.430
If you come with us, we won't hurt any of them.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.140
Not that they'll survive long either way.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.530
Daichi?

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.240
Where do you think you're going, pretty boy?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.740
You're trying too hard to look tough.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:47.700
You belong here, with all of us!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:51.710
Daichi!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.000
What do you think you can do here, Earthling?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.630
I'm saying...

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.590
He's...

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.010
Teppei is one of us!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.310
<i>Neoteny?!</i>

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:19.320
I won't let you have Teppei!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.920
Moco, he got me...

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.890
We're leaving.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.400
I've never seen that Livlaster before.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.280
That isn't the one from Blume.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.900
It may have materialized here.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.700
That'd make it the Livlaster Tanegashima.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.040
But I can't believe a neoteny appeared
from one of the Earthlings.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.910
Maybe Albion really does intend to betray us?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.630
He couldn't even if he wanted to.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.670
The feeling of being a Kill-T-Gang...

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:23.300
It's a sense of pleasure so intense that he'll never be able to give it up.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.140
They're terrifying opponents.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.360
They looked like a couple of teenagers.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:42.110
Are those the enemies we've been fighting?

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:43.740
It doesn't matter what they look like—

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:48.160
if their Kill-T-Gangs reach Earth,

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.780
it's all over.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.910
Oh, welcome back.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.670
Akari's amazing, Commander.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.670
She's the one who brought our defense system back online.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.050
She did?

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.010
So? Where is she?

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:07.630
She said she was tired and went home.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.600
Yomatsuri Akari.

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.890
Arashi Teppei.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:15.100
Mutou Hana.

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:17.480
And Manatsu Daichi.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:20.270
What do you think, Science Chief?

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:22.570
What do you mean?

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:25.610
When you look at them, don't you feel something?

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.110
Feel something?

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:34.540
I can't say that I've any empirical evidence of that nature.

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:38.210
You want to feel something, don't you?

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:40.920
You want to see something in them.

00:24:14.260 --> 00:24:17.720
The Kivotos Plan team is in an artificial sleep

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.890
aboard the Globe Orbital Base <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:23.400
One of them, the person who gave Teppei their genes,

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:25.690
is targeted by strange enemy spies.

00:24:26.690 --> 00:24:28.440
Teppei decides to...

00:24:28.860 --> 00:24:31.490
Next time, on episode 5 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:33.280
Starry Sky's Picture Book.

00:24:33.910 --> 00:24:36.740
Earth Engine, expand!
